{"backgroundInformation":"This model is used at the University of Nevada at Las Vegas as part of the undergraduate introductory Environmental Science course. It is a minor modification of a model originally built by Erik Pruyt at Delft University of Technology (the Netherlands) and used in their Introductory System Dynamics course. You are the Game Warden for an island which is experiencing an explosion in its rabbit population. In order to keep the population within SUSTAINABLE bounds (estimated to be a population of 500 rabbits) it has been decided to introduce some predators, specifically foxes, to the island. The simulation lasts 50 years. When it begins, the island is without foxes. Each year thereafter, you can either release foxes onto the island or remove them from the island (either by shooting them or humanely trapping them for return to the mainland). It is your task to stabilize the populations of both animals.","@type":"XMILEModel","modelId":"Rabbits_and_foxes","sourceFile":"Rabbits_and_foxes.xmile","simSpecs":{"method":"RK4","time_units":"Year","start":"0","stop":"50","dt":"0.25"},"variables":[{"type":"stock","name":"Estimated_Rabbit_Population","units":"Rabbit","eqn":"initial_rabbit_population","inflows":["rabbit births"],"outflows":["rabbit deaths"]},{"type":"stock","name":"Fox_Population","units":"Fox","eqn":"initial_fox_population","inflows":["fox births"],"outflows":["fox deaths"]},{"type":"aux","name":"additional_foxes","units":"","eqn":"GAME ( 0)"},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_births","units":"Fox/Year","eqn":"Fox_Population * fox_birth_rate + additional_foxes"},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_consumption_of_rabbits","units":"Rabbit/Year","eqn":"Fox_Population * fox_food_requirements * fox_rabbit_consumption_lookup(rabbit_crowding)"},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_deaths","units":"Fox/Year","eqn":"Fox_Population / average_fox_life * fox_mortality_lookup(fox_food_availability) + MIN(healthy_foxes_shot, Fox_Population-Fox_Population / average_fox_life * fox_mortality_lookup(fox_food_availability))"},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_food_availability","units":"Dmnl","eqn":"fox_consumption_of_rabbits/(MAX(Fox_Population,1) * fox_food_requirements)"},{"type":"aux","name":"healthy_foxes_shot","units":"Fox/Year","eqn":"GAME ( 0)"},{"type":"aux","name":"initial_fox_population","units":"Fox","eqn":"GAME ( 0)"},{"type":"aux","name":"rabbit_births","units":"Rabbit/Year","eqn":"Estimated_Rabbit_Population * rabbit_birth_rate +\"Up/Down_Estimated_Rabbit_Population\""},{"type":"aux","name":"rabbit_crowding","units":"Dmnl","eqn":"Estimated_Rabbit_Population/carrying_capacity"},{"type":"aux","name":"rabbit_deaths","units":"Rabbit/Year","eqn":"MAX(Estimated_Rabbit_Population / average_rabbit_life * effect_of_crowding_on_deaths_lookup(rabbit_crowding), fox_consumption_of_rabbits)"},{"type":"aux","name":"Up/Down_Estimated_Rabbit_Population","units":"Rabbit/Year","eqn":"GAME ( 0)"},{"type":"aux","name":"effect_of_crowding_on_deaths_lookup","units":"Dmnl","eqn":""},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_mortality_lookup","units":"Dmnl","eqn":""},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_rabbit_consumption_lookup","units":"Dmnl","eqn":""},{"type":"aux","name":"average_fox_life","units":"Year","eqn":"4"},{"type":"aux","name":"average_rabbit_life","units":"Year","eqn":"2"},{"type":"aux","name":"carrying_capacity","units":"Rabbit","eqn":"500"},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_birth_rate","units":"1/Year","eqn":"0.25"},{"type":"aux","name":"fox_food_requirements","units":"Rabbit/(Fox*Year)","eqn":"25"},{"type":"aux","name":"initial_rabbit_population","units":"Rabbit","eqn":"500"},{"type":"aux","name":"rabbit_birth_rate","units":"1/Year","eqn":"2"}]}